{
  "_readme": [
    "Which Vercel project every local repo — or monorepo app directory — deploys as, and",
    "under which of the estate's three Vercel teams. Committed, and deliberately free of",
    "secrets: names only, no tokens and no values. The per-team API tokens live in the",
    "environment (see `teams[].token_env`), never here and never in git.",
    "",
    "`path` is relative to `projects/` and is the directory that gets the `.vercel/` link",
    "and, later in the epic, the generated `.env.local`. Its first segment is always the",
    "local repo directory; anything after it is the Vercel project's Root Directory, so a",
    "monorepo fans out into one entry per app (jamienisbet -> 3, sustentus -> 8,",
    "remi-ai -> 6) and a single-app repo whose code sits in a subdirectory (agorasim,",
    "barzinho) points at that subdirectory rather than at the repo root.",
    "",
    "`project` is the Vercel project NAME, which is all `vercel link --project` needs;",
    "project IDs are deliberately omitted so a rename is a one-word edit here. Names drift",
    "from repo names freely — barzinho -> barzinho-proposal, messy-play ->",
    "happymessmakers, kau-american-bbq -> kau, dungeons-dragons -> dungeons-dragons-mafra,",
    "sustentus apps/console -> tenant-management — so this mapping is not derivable and",
    "that is the whole reason the file exists.",
    "",
    "Captured 2026-09-05 from the live estate: the Vercel API's project list per team",
    "(each project's linked GitHub repo is what pins it to a local directory) plus each",
    "project's Root Directory setting. Regenerate the same way when it drifts; env-audit",
    "(epic vercel-env-system) is what will notice that it has."
  ],
